11.0.0 — a key held through the loop's wrap sounds on; other makers' Audio Units in the lists; a Samples folder to hear sounds from before placing them; the top bar in two rows on most iPhones in portrait, with the Echoelmusic mark

What is new since 10073. Each line is code that the Echoel Studio run builds; the rules have tests
of their own, and nothing here is device-verified yet.
- Playing live: a key held on the screen (piano keys, hex cells, chord pads) or on a MIDI keyboard
  sounds on when the song loop wraps, when you seek while the song plays, and when a MIDI clock, a
  timecode or a Jam moves the playing song to keep it in step; on that track only the song's own
  notes end there. The track is still cleared as before when it arpeggiates (the arpeggio of the
  keys you hold plays on), when its clip moved a controller or the pitch wheel, and when the live
  sustain pedal holds one of the song's notes; in those last two the held key ends too. With every
  key up, notes that only the pedal holds end there as well. A clip note on the key's own pitch
  ends the key with it. Launching or stopping a clip on that track still ends the key. Stop, a
  pause and a seek while stopped end every sounding note, as before; on a track that arpeggiates,
  keys still held go on arpeggiating.
- Playing live: a key pressed before its track begins to arpeggiate ends when you let go of it.
  With MPE Out sending to a device, choosing another track for the keys sends that device all
  notes off once, so a note held across the change does not hang there.
- Audio Units: the Sound page's "Audio Unit Instrument" list and the "Add Effect" list (Mixer → a
  track's Effects) now read the installed instruments and audio effects two ways, through the
  system's list of plugins and by asking the system for each registered unit directly, and show a
  unit found both ways once, under its maker ("Other" where the system names none; one used lately
  also shows under "Recent"). The list is read again each time it opens. Whether other makers'
  units, missing until now, appear is check 2. MIDI effects and generators are not listed. As
  before, Echoelmusic's own units are not listed again among them: Add Effect shows Echoelmusic's
  effects first, under "Echoelmusic".
- Browser (Song menu → Browser…): it also lists the Samples folder, which it makes the first time
  it opens; from then on the Files app shows it as Echoelmusic › Samples (under On My iPhone or On
  My iPad). Subfolders are included: each sound is listed by its name, with "Samples › Drums" in
  the line under it. From the Samples folder it lists up to 2,000 sounds, only files that open as
  audio, and says so when the folder holds more; nothing there is changed or removed, and placing
  a sound copies it into the song. A tap on a sound's name plays it, as its Listen button does, and
  a second tap stops it; a sound from outside the open song, as every Samples sound is, plays its
  first half minute. VoiceOver reads a sound's name and details as one button, apart from its
  Listen and Place buttons. The browser reads again when you come back from the Files app, and on
  pull to refresh.
- Top bar: on an iPhone in portrait it keeps two rows, with the tempo in the second, where it fell
  to a third; the tool tiles there are narrower, 44 points wide instead of 60, and so is the area
  that takes their taps; their height is unchanged. While the Heart Rate Strap, the Camera or Apple
  Health is the body source, the pulse there shows the heart with its number, or a dash where its
  words stood. On the iPhone SE, 12 mini, 13 mini, XS and 11 Pro (screens 375 points wide) it stays
  three rows at the standard text size, and a larger text size or Display Zoom can give another
  iPhone three rows too. A long song name is cut short instead of adding a row. On an 11-inch iPad
  in landscape the bar can now take two rows where it took one, to make room for the mark.
- The Echoelmusic mark, the E over three waves of the app icon, is back: at the front of the song
  menu, which it opens, and at the top of About.

Known limit: a MIDI take does not record a key held across the loop's end as it was heard. While
the record line shows "Loop Record · take n" (a loop of two bars or longer), the note ends at the
loop's end and the next take does not have it. On a one-bar loop, a key let go after the loop
came round is recorded shorter than it was held.

Previous: 11.0.0 (10073) — touch loudness, slice pads, the chords of the song's key; 10072 — the
video window dims footage that strobes. Earlier: git history.

Bump this file on a commit whose "Echoel Studio" run is green to upload a build
(.github/workflows/studio-testflight.yml). Build number = 10000 + the workflow's run number.
The version is MARKETING_VERSION in EchoelStudio/project.yml.
This file is a test list for the device, not a source for claims (ContentPipeline/CLAIMS.md).

Five things to try on the device (answer each yes or no):
1. Loop on, a synth track on the Init sound or Warm Pad with its Arpeggiator off, whose clip has
   notes only (drawn, or played on the screen keys: a take from a MIDI keyboard keeps its pedal and
   wheel, and then the key ends at the wrap, as stated above). Without the sustain pedal, hold a key
   the clip never plays (on the screen keys or a MIDI keyboard) across the loop's end. Does it sound
   on without a click while the song's notes start again, and end when you let go? With a MIDI
   keyboard, also tap Arrange's ruler while holding: does the key sound on there too?
2. With an AUv3 instrument or effect of another maker installed that another host app on this
   device already lists: an instrument track's Sound page → Audio Unit Instrument, or Mixer → a
   track's Effects → Add Effect. Is it listed below "Audio Units" (in its maker's section or under
   "Other"), and when you choose it, does it load and sound? For a no, say which: not listed, or
   listed but did not load (and the message shown).
3. Song menu → Browser… once, then close it: this makes the Samples folder. Files app → On My
   iPhone → Echoelmusic → Samples: put a folder of a few WAV files there, come back to
   Echoelmusic, Song menu → Browser…. Is each listed by its name, with "Samples › <folder>" in the
   line under it, does a tap on a name play it (half a minute at most) and a second tap stop it,
   and can you place one on a track?
4. iPhone in portrait, text size and Display Zoom at their defaults: is the top bar two rows, with
   the tempo in the second, and are its tiles still easy to hit? (On an iPhone SE, 12 mini,
   13 mini, XS or 11 Pro, three rows are expected.) Does the Echoelmusic mark at its front open the
   song menu?
5. With VoiceOver on, in the Browser: does a sound's name read as a button, and does a double tap
   play it and a second one stop it?
